-point/id #uuid "2ba5d861-c6bf-57df-aa00-7034aeb5e1ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Supplementary Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c351bb0b-5f84-561f-8fa5-737f86584966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "133" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c351bb0b-5f84-561f-8fa5-737f86584966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "133" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503373} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb22d846-456e-5766-8b0e-26165fc31370" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0518b35-857c-5bdb-a223-e7f6be6165f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-237185" :question/problem "![](images/78/78d588198d35e69ca7ae2b199dd52d2c07e5c9d3268214821b737deffe5cb03d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠BOE?$\n\n$m∠BOE=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d3/d3ba77dd51c7d26685246304088d484144f5dcda57c424656ae305cc2ffa78ae.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠COB$ and $∠BOE$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠COB+m∠BOE={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠BOE$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOE & ={180}^{∘}-m∠COB \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={133}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110627 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "931f7270-ec55-5c42-8c1b-6c7988f6c921" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Supplementary Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023afd58-8f3f-580d-8449-3aa50a35e580" :answer/type {:d