}{AD}$ is a segment, we have that $∠BOA$ and $∠BOD$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠BOA+m∠BOD={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠BOD$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠BOA \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{132}^{∘} \\\\  & ={48}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ba5d861-c6bf-57df-aa00-7034aeb5e1ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Supplementary Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ca6621c-07b4-5673-90fb-156c9dd985c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "113" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ca6621c-07b4-5673-90fb-156c9dd985c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "113" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503236} :answer-field/id #uuid "4000a1f5-32a2-5471-9f90-0bfc3b4839fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a68d95ce-c563-5215-b1b0-c9bfcf7d73e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-237390" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e8f3df43e45dd6916a35c3e9a41fb517f94d32591f656628c5723fd4d0f754d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠DOC?$\n\n$m∠DOC=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/4f/4f0f4b52fc5b84d2d63281da0bc8d92f7433a248550e81c27b0a92a6e5d58a34.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠DOE$ and $∠DOC$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠DOE+m∠DOC={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠DOC$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠DOC & ={180}^{∘}-m∠DOE \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{67}^{∘} \\\\  & ={113}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ba5d861-c6bf-57df-aa00-7034aeb5e1ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Supplementary Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba26f4fc-9b25-5012-9058-68aac89a4425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba26f4fc-9b25-5012-9058-68aac89a4425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503358} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3c733f8-5234-5f95-ab08-5696cfa175b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6af619db-0f0f-58ae-bb63-22eb9d582800" :question/math-academy-id "q-237400" :question/problem "![](images/79/795f457314076b565d76a6b2579f2e1f87a247053dd0bb5de72225d63e17bf7f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠COD?$\n\n$m∠COD=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/70/7045c84435a9ed2934569aceabf9d01e01d4278de6b89329664b654dc53b5250.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠COD$ and $∠DOE$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠COD+m∠DOE={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠COD$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠DOE \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{144}^{∘} \\\\  & ={36}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c7eec3a-50e3-5550-9e1e-def64ca9642a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Supplementary Angles From a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c185cc5-4f85-5664-a619-1b09f768c62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c185cc5-4f85-5664-a619-1b09f768c62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503126} :answer-field/id #uuid "e82aee16-2622-55e0-a5db-cad4413860c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e08860ba-c89a-5bab-9100-e207695170f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-237426" :question/problem "The measure of the angle that forms a linear pair with the angle of ${27}^{∘}$ is{{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "If two angles form a linear pair, the sum of their measures is equal to ${180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the measure of an angle forming a linear pair with an angle of ${27}^{∘}$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}-{27}^{∘} & ={153}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110627 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "931f7270-ec55-5c42-8c1b-6c7988f6c921" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Supplementary Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b12c064-a152-5a88-95eb-43a15a8d4791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠BFE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503007} {:answer/id #uuid "57184e40-d1eb-50e7-b32f-c69d102cd576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠BFA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503150} {:answer/id #uuid "714c4364-8e8d-5633-8878-a0c75b4069ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454